# The frappe this project builds against, everywhere. The single source of
# truth: scripts/init.sh (devcontainer), .github/helper/install.sh (server
# tests), ui-tests.yml, migration-test.yml and builds.yml (the published image)
# all resolve frappe through here, via scripts/fetch-frappe.sh.
#
# Nothing consumes FRAPPE_REF directly as a git ref, because nothing can:
# `bench init --frappe-branch` becomes `git clone --branch`, which takes a
# branch or a tag and never a commit. fetch-frappe.sh clones the commit and
# parks it on FRAPPE_PIN_BRANCH so bench has a name to ask for. builds.yml goes
# one step further and copies that clone into the builder image, because the
# Containerfile clones from a path inside the container.
#
# Pinned to a commit, not a branch. `develop` moves under us: two builds a week
# apart contained different framework code with no way to reconstruct the
# earlier one, which is the question a customer bug report actually asks.
#
# This previously pointed at Absolute-Insight/frappe@vectora, a fork that was
# never created -- the org holds only simcrm. GitHub 404s a missing repo the
# same way it 404s a private one, so git asked for a username, found no TTY and
# died with "could not read Username for 'https://github.com'". That killed
# `set -e` scripts before bench init in the devcontainer and broke the server,
# migration and e2e lanes in CI.
#
# To move the pin: pick a frappe commit, check the suite is green on it, and
# change FRAPPE_REF here only. Keep it inside pyproject's
# [tool.bench.frappe-dependencies] range (>=16.0.0-dev,<=17.0.0-dev).
FRAPPE_REPO="${FRAPPE_REPO:-https://github.com/frappe/frappe}"

# frappe/frappe develop @ 2026-08-30, __version__ 17.0.0-dev -- the last develop
# commit before this suite's most recent green server-tests run.
FRAPPE_REF="${FRAPPE_REF:-e2e1006be48417dc8b4b12eeab9bd8d148587893}"

# A commit is not a branch, and `bench init --frappe-branch` only takes a branch
# name. The clone below is parked on this local branch so bench has one to ask
# for; it never leaves this machine.
FRAPPE_PIN_BRANCH="${FRAPPE_PIN_BRANCH:-pinned}"
